## Background and Motivation

`QuicServerConnectionOptions` in `System.Net.Quic` has added `DefaultCloseErrorCode` and `DefaultStreamErrorCode`. These are the error codes sent to the client when an error occurs, and there isn't an error code explicitly specified, e.g. the connection closes and it wasn't caused by `QuicConnection.CloseAsync(errorCode: xxx)`.

Also, I noticed the final API on `QuicServerConnectionOptions` changed the max stream types from `ushort` to `int`. Our options should also change.

## Proposed API

```diff
namespace Microsoft.AspNetCore.Server.Kestrel.Transport.Quic;

public class QuicTransportOptions
{
    /// <summary>
    /// The maximum number of concurrent bi-directional streams per connection.
    /// </summary>
-   public ushort MaxBidirectionalStreamCount { get; set; } = 100;
+   public int MaxBidirectionalStreamCount { get; set; } = 100;

    /// <summary>
    /// The maximum number of concurrent inbound uni-directional streams per connection.
    /// </summary>
-   public ushort MaxUnidirectionalStreamCount { get; set; } = 10;
+   public int MaxUnidirectionalStreamCount { get; set; } = 10;

+   /// <summary>
+   /// Error code used when the stream needs to abort the read or write side of the stream internally.
+   /// </summary>
+   // Setter will validate value is in the required range (between 0 and (1L << 62) - 1)
+   public long DefaultStreamErrorCode { get; set; } = 0;

+   /// <summary>
+   /// Error code used when an open connection is disposed.
+   /// </summary>
+   // Setter will validate value is in the required range (between 0 and (1L << 62) - 1)
+   public long DefaultCloseErrorCode { get; set; } = 0;
}
```

